WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.667
The target box measures four by two units. The prediction is shifted by one unit.

2
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:14.517
The intersection has area six and the union area ten.

3
00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:22.183
IoU is 0.6: recognizing the class alone would not measure this localization error.

4
00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:29.533
Two images are paired with two captions using the same object names.

5
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:36.383
Reversing above and below changes the correct matching.

6
00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:43.733
Compositional evaluation requires the crossed relations, not only object recognition.

7
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:51.083
The answer claims that order B totals twenty.

8
00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:58.250
Twenty appears in the table but belongs to order A; B totals thirty.

9
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:06.300
The test must validate row, column and value to detect a plausible but false answer.

10
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:13.650
Sequence A turns on a light and then opens a door.

11
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:20.500
Sequence B contains the same events in the opposite order.

12
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:28.167
A temporal test must distinguish them even when their object and action inventories match.

13
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:35.517
The question asks how many dots are in the image; its text stays identical.

14
00:01:35.517 --> 00:01:42.683
Only the image changes from two dots to three, while other conditions are held fixed.

15
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:51.100
The answer must change; always answering two can reveal reliance on text rather than the image.

16
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:58.450
Five cases have confidence scores, but some answers are incorrect.

17
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:07.133
A high threshold accepts two with no errors here; lowering it accepts four with one error.

18
00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:14.800
Report coverage and error together: two successes do not prove reliability beyond this sample.

